--- a/docs/quickstart.md
+++ b/docs/quickstart.md
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ ## 2. Open a database
 ```sh
 sqlmux ./app.db
 sqlmux "postgres://me@localhost:5432/app?sslmode=disable"
+sqlmux "gaussdb://me@db.example:8000/app?sslmode=prefer"   # also opengauss://
 sqlmux "mysql://me@localhost:3306/app"
 sqlmux "redis://localhost:6379/0"
 ```
@@ -42,7 +43,7 @@ ## 2. Open a database
 ```toml
 [[connection]]
 name         = "local"
-engine       = "postgres"          # postgres | mysql | sqlite | mssql | redis
+engine       = "postgres"          # postgres | gaussdb | mysql | sqlite | mssql | redis
 dsn          = "postgres://me@localhost:5432/app?sslmode=disable"
 password_env = "PGPASSWORD"        # or password_cmd = "…", or password = "…"
 ```
@@ -59,6 +60,8 @@ ## 2. Open a database
 
 Running `sqlmux` with no connections opens a form instead (name, engine, host, port, user, password, database); its password goes to the OS keychain. All the connection fields are in [Configuration](config.md#connectionstoml).
 
+For PostgreSQL-protocol GaussDB or openGauss, choose `gaussdb` in the form, or set `engine = "gaussdb"` in the file. Set the instance's actual port (the form suggests 8000). This uses native GaussDB SHA256 authentication rather than the PostgreSQL driver. GaussDB(for MySQL) uses `mysql`. See [GaussDB connections](config.md#gaussdb-and-opengauss) for TLS, credentials and the supported authentication methods.
+
 ## 3. Your first table
 
 The window has three panes: the schema tree on the left, a data pane, and a query on the right.
